  "steps": [
    "Preheat the oven to 400°F (200°C). Line a large rimmed baking sheet with parchment paper.",
    "Place the trimmed asparagus in a single layer on one side of the prepared baking sheet. Drizzle with 1 tablespoon of olive oil, and toss to coat evenly.",
    "Pat the salmon fillets dry with paper towels and place them on the other side of the baking sheet.",
    "Brush the salmon fillets with the remaining 1 tablespoon of olive oil. In a small bowl, mix together the Cajun seasoning, garlic powder, and kosher salt, then rub the spice blend evenly over the top of each salmon fillet.",
    "Arrange the lemon slices around the salmon and asparagus on the sheet pan.",
    "Roast in the preheated oven at 400°F (200°C) for 12 to 15 minutes, until the asparagus is tender-crisp and bright green, and the salmon flakes easily with a fork and reaches an internal temperature of 145°F (63°C).",
    "Remove from the oven, squeeze roasted lemon juice over the top, and serve immediately."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Ensure your salmon fillets are uniform in thickness so they cook at the exact same rate.",
    "Store leftovers in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.",
    "Swap asparagus for green beans or broccoli florets if desired, adjusting roast time by a couple of minutes."
  ],
  "storage": "Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days. Reheat gently in a skillet or microwave.",
